tly recorded as a stated assumption before the final estimate is produced."},{"kind":"error","text":"If the final estimate is produced without either a client answer or a documented assumption for an open question, treat the estimate as invalid/provisional."}],"id":"76-open-questions-dependency","readingChosen":"Treated as a process gate: estimation/final scope cannot be finalized while open questions remain unresolved."}]},{"spans":[{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Estimate document contains a separate effort line (hours/days) for each checklist item under Product/UX, Frontend, Backend, Integrations, QA, DevOps and Documentation."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Estimate is not expressed solely as a per-screen count; screen-count figures, if present, are supplementary to the itemised breakdown."},{"kind":"error","text":"If an estimate omits any checklist item, it is rejected/flagged as incomplete before being sent to the client."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Each itemised estimate line can be reviewed, approved, or revised independently of the others."}],"id":"74-estimation-checklist","readingChosen":"Treated as a process requirement: the estimate deliverable must break down effort by each listed item rather than by screen/page count."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"Proposal document lists a chosen option for each of: frontend framework, backend framework, database, authentication approach, file storage, email integration, PDF generation approach, hosting/cloud platform, CI/CD, monitoring/logging."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Each proposed technology choice is accompanied by a justification referencing expected scale and the 7-year data-retention requirement."},{"kind":"error","text":"A proposal that omits a justification tying the database/storage choice to 7-year retention is flagged as incomplete and returned for revision."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only the implementation team (not the client) is responsible for drafting the technology proposal; client approval is required before the stack is finalised."}],"id":"75-technology-stack","readingChosen":"The implementation team must produce and submit a written technology proposal covering each listed concern before build starts."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer enters valid credentials → is authenticated and redirected to their account/catalogue area."},{"kind":"error","text":"Customer enters invalid credentials → sees an error message and is not logged in; account lockout/rate-limiting applies after repeated failures."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Users are assigned roles (e.g., customer, staff, admin) and each role sees only the features/screens/data permitted for that role."},{"kind":"error","text":"A user attempting to access a page or action outside their role's permission is blocked and shown an access-denied response."},{"kind":"data","text":"Login attempts and role assignments are recorded for later audit."}],"id":"76-customer-auth-and-access","readingChosen":"Covers login/registration for customers plus role-based permission enforcement across the portal."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Staff/admin can create, edit, and deactivate a customer or company record, with changes saved and reflected immediately in listings."},{"kind":"data","text":"Each customer record is linked to a company record enabling company-specific pricing and order history."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to save a company/customer record with missing required fields (e.g., name) is rejected with a validation error."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Only staff/admin roles can create or deactivate customer/company records; customers cannot edit other customers' data."}],"id":"76-customer-company-management","readingChosen":"Staff/admin can create and manage customer accounts and associated companies, including multi-user companies."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer browses the product catalogue and sees paginated product listings with images, names, and prices."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer enters a search term → matching products are returned; applying a category filter narrows results further."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer selects a vehicle (make/model/year) → only parts compatible with that vehicle are shown."},{"kind":"error","text":"Search with no matching results shows an explicit empty-state message rather than a blank page."},{"kind":"error","text":"Vehicle compatibility search with no matches informs the customer no compatible parts were found."}],"id":"76-catalogue-search-vehicle-compatibility","readingChosen":"Covers browsing the product catalogue, free-text search, category filtering, and searching by vehicle to find compatible parts."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Logged-in customer viewing a product sees the price associated with their company's assigned price list."},{"kind":"data","text":"Price-list assignments are stored per company and applied consistently across catalogue, basket, and checkout."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a product has no price entry for the customer's price list, the product is shown as unavailable/priced-on-request rather than showing an incorrect price."},{"kind":"permission","text":"Customers can only see their own company's prices; they cannot view or infer another company's pricing."}],"id":"76-customer-specific-pricing","readingChosen":"Prices shown to a logged-in customer reflect their company's negotiated price list rather than a single public price."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"A valid ERP CSV file is imported and stock quantities/availability are updated for matching product SKUs."},{"kind":"error","text":"An import file with malformed rows or unknown SKUs is rejected (or partially processed) and an error report is generated listing the failed rows."},{"kind":"data","text":"Each import run is logged with timestamp, file name, number of records processed, and number of failures."},{"kind":"error","text":"If stock for a product drops to zero, the product is marked out-of-stock and cannot be added to a basket."}],"id":"76-erp-stock-import","readingChosen":"Stock levels are imported from the client's ERP system via scheduled/periodic CSV import rather than real-time API sync."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer adds a product to the basket → basket quantity and total update immediately."},{"kind":"error","text":"Customer attempts to add more units than are in stock → is blocked or quantity is capped with a warning message."},{"kind":"happy","text":"At checkout, customer selects a delivery date/slot limited to options allowed by configured delivery scheduling rules (e.g., cut-off times, blackout days)."},{"kind":"error","text":"Checkout with an empty basket or missing required address/payment information is blocked with a validation error."},{"kind":"data","text":"Successful checkout creates an order record linked to the customer, basket contents, delivery slot, and totals."}],"id":"76-basket-checkout-delivery-scheduling","readingChosen":"Customers add items to a basket, proceed through checkout, and delivery date/slot options are constrained by configured scheduling rules."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer places an order → receives an order confirmation with order number and status 'placed'."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer views order history listing all past orders with status and date; selecting one shows full order detail."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer can track an order's current status (e.g., processing, dispatched, delivered)."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer cancels an eligible order → order status changes to 'cancelled' and relevant stock/invoice adjustments occur."},{"kind":"error","text":"Attempting to cancel an order that has already progressed past the cancellable stage (e.g., dispatched) is rejected with an explanatory message."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Customer selects 'repeat order' on a past order → a new basket is pre-populated with the same